<!-- Extend lines with several verses.
     P1 m1: verse 1 holds "Joy" over three notes (extend) while verse 2 has a syllable on each of them.
     P1 m2: verse 2 ends with an extend on "ye" and isn't sung again, while verse 1 goes on.
     P1 m3-m5: verse 3 holds "Lo" over m3 (extend), m4 is sung only in verse 1 (e.g. a first ending), verse 3 goes on in m5.
     P2 m1: voice 1 holds "Hold" (verse 1, extend) over two notes, then rests while voice 2 sings verse 2. -->
